    "body": "Thank you for this report and for the test file.\n\nTriage: `P3`, `effort:high`. The refusal is safe, because CamCraft does not post a path that cuts into the part. But it is wrong behaviour: a contour with an inside corner that is sharper than the tool radius is a legal program. The tool must leave the corner radius in the material and continue, not refuse the whole run. The current workaround is in the message: select the closed ring, or use a smaller tool.\n\nA `P3` is worked before planned work. An agent starts on it now with your `2d_contour_test.zip`. Another user reported the same refusal on an open chain, so the fix will cover both cases.\n\nIf you can, please tell us one thing: did you select the whole outline (a closed ring), or some edges only (an open chain)?\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
